---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CuriosityGenerator from '../components/CuriosityGenerator';
import SurveyDashboard from '../components/SurveyDashboard';
import HeroObservation from '../components/HeroObservation.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import hero from '../assets/featured-orange-mushrooms.png';
import explore from '../assets/pathways/explore.jpg';
import curious from '../assets/pathways/curious.jpg';
import investigate from '../assets/pathways/investigate.jpg';
import connect from '../assets/pathways/connect.jpg';

const paths=[
  {name:'Discover',href:'/discover/',desc:'Stories and observations from the fungal world.',icon:'◎'},
  {name:'Learn',href:'/learn/',desc:'Practice noticing. Follow a new question.',icon:'◇'},
  {name:'Investigate',href:'/investigate/',desc:'Research methods, original evidence and tools.',icon:'▥'},
  {name:'Connect',href:'/connect/',desc:'Find collaborators and curious people.',icon:'♧'}
];
---
<Base title="See fungi differently" description="MycoView is a welcoming field station for fungal discovery, citizen science, original evidence, research tools, and meaningful collaboration.">
<div class="mv-home">
  <section class="mv-hero" aria-labelledby="mv-hero-title">
    <div class="mv-hero-image"><Image src={hero} alt="Brilliant orange wild mushrooms emerging among moss and leaves" loading="eager" widths={[640,960,1440]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 53vw" /><HeroObservation /></div>
    <div class="mv-hero-copy">
      <p class="mv-kicker">WELCOME TO MYCOVIEW · AN INDEPENDENT MYCOLOGY FIELD STATION</p>
      <h1 id="mv-hero-title">See fungi <em>differently.</em></h1>
      <p class="mv-hero-lead">The fungal world is full of unanswered questions. Come explore it through field discoveries, practical science, and the people who make curiosity contagious.</p>
      <div class="mv-hero-actions"><a class="mv-primary" href="#start">Start exploring <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a><a class="mv-secondary" href="/investigate/">Follow the evidence →</a></div>
      <p class="mv-hero-aside">No credentials required. Just curiosity.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="mv-pathways" aria-label="Ways to explore MycoView">
    {paths.map(p=><a href={p.href} class="mv-pathway"><span class="mv-pathway-icon" aria-hidden="true">{p.icon}</span><span><strong>{p.name}</strong><small>{p.desc}</small></span><span class="mv-pathway-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>)}
  </nav>

  <section id="start" class="mv-section mv-opening" aria-labelledby="mv-opening-title">
    <div class="mv-opening-intro"><p class="mv-kicker">THE QUESTION IS THE BEGINNING</p><h2 id="mv-opening-title">The woods don't care about your credentials.</h2><p>But they reward attention. A mushroom you can't name, a pattern you can't explain, a person who sees something you've missed—each is a beginning. Start wherever you are. Go as deep as you like.</p><a href="/learn/" class="mv-inline-link">Try a different way of looking →</a></div>
    <div class="mv-opening-image"><Image src={curious} alt="Detailed purple gills of a wild mushroom seen from below" widths={[460,800]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 42vw" loading="lazy"/><span>LOOK CLOSER · THE DETAILS CHANGE THE STORY</span></div>
  </section>

  <section class="mv-section mv-discovery" aria-labelledby="mv-discovery-title">
    <div class="mv-section-head"><div><p class="mv-kicker">WHAT'S HAPPENING AT THE FIELD STATION</p><h2 id="mv-discovery-title">An observation is only the beginning.</h2></div><a href="/investigate/" class="mv-inline-link">Visit Investigate →</a></div>
    <div class="mv-discovery-grid">
      <article class="mv-story-feature">
        <div class="mv-story-image"><Image src={investigate} alt="A camera documenting a cluster of mushrooms in the forest" widths={[440,760]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 35vw" loading="lazy"/></div>
        <div class="mv-story-copy"><p class="mv-kicker">FEATURED INVESTIGATION · TAXONOMY & EVIDENCE</p><h3>When does a name outrun the evidence?</h3><p>What can a photograph really tell us about a species? Explore provisional names, DNA barcodes, and why a confident identification isn't always the same as a well-supported one.</p><a href="/investigate/learn/#my-inat" class="mv-inline-link">Follow the question →</a></div>
      </article>
      <article class="mv-play"><p class="mv-kicker">TRY SOMETHING UNEXPECTED</p><h3>The Curiosity Generator</h3><p>Small, playful experiments to notice what you might otherwise miss. No scores. No leaderboard. No wrong starting point.</p><CuriosityGenerator client:visible /><a class="mv-inline-link" href="/learn/">Keep getting curious →</a></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mv-host-section" aria-labelledby="mv-host-title">
    <div class="mv-host-inner">
      <div class="mv-host-image"><Image src={connect} alt="Naturalists gathered in the forest, examining a discovery together" widths={[560,900]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 45vw" loading="lazy"/><span>REAL PEOPLE. SHARED QUESTIONS.</span></div>
      <div class="mv-host-copy"><p class="mv-kicker">MEET YOUR GUIDE</p><h2 id="mv-host-title">Hi, I'm MycoGeeky.</h2><p class="mv-host-quote">I spend an unreasonable amount of time asking questions about fungi, chasing mushrooms through forests, and talking to people who know considerably more than I do.</p><p>This is where I share what we're discovering, build tools to help us investigate, and invite you to join the adventure. The best part isn't collecting answers. It's finding people worth asking questions with.</p><div class="mv-host-links"><a class="mv-inline-link" href="/about/">Get to know your guide →</a><a class="mv-inline-link" href="/connect/">Find your people →</a></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mv-section mv-research" aria-labelledby="mv-research-title">
    <div class="mv-section-head"><div><p class="mv-kicker">FROM WONDER TO EVIDENCE</p><h2 id="mv-research-title">Real questions deserve real tools.</h2><p>Learn how to evaluate a claim, trace an original source, or participate in a growing body of field observations. You can learn the methods before you ever open a workbench.</p></div><a href="/investigate/#workbench" class="mv-inline-link">Explore the research workbench →</a></div>
    <div class="mv-study-feature"><div><p class="mv-kicker">RESEARCH NAVIGATOR / FIFTEEN FRAMEWORKS</p><h3>What would it take to find out?</h3><p>Explore fifteen guided research frameworks across ecology, taxonomy, morphology, molecular evidence, and biodiversity. Discover appropriate methods, limitations, and next steps.</p></div><a class="mv-primary mv-discovery-invite" href="/investigate/study-designer/">Explore the Research Navigator <span class="mv-discovery-indicator" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="mv-research-grid">
      <a href="/investigate/resources/" class="mv-research-card"><span class="mv-card-number">01 / RESEARCH SOURCES</span><h3>Find the original evidence.</h3><p>Names, specimens, literature and sequence databases—with context for when each is useful.</p><span>Open research resources ↗</span></a>
      <a href="/investigate/learn/" class="mv-research-card"><span class="mv-card-number">02 / LEARN THE METHODS</span><h3>Learn to think like a mycologist.</h3><p>From field notes to collection curation, find out what makes an observation scientifically useful.</p><span>Explore the methods ↗</span></a>
      <div class="mv-survey-card"><p class="mv-card-number">03 / FIELD DATA · LIVE PROJECT</p><SurveyDashboard client:visible /><a href="/investigate/learn/#surveys" class="mv-inline-link">Explore the survey →</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mv-section mv-community" aria-labelledby="mv-community-title">
    <div class="mv-community-image"><Image src={explore} alt="Woodland and sandstone cliffs along a hiking trail" widths={[500,850]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 46vw" loading="lazy"/></div>
    <div class="mv-community-copy"><p class="mv-kicker">THE CONVERSATION CONTINUES</p><h2 id="mv-community-title">Come for the mushrooms. Stay for the people.</h2><p>The MycoView brings conversations, field stories and science to video. Neo Myco turns shared questions into collaborative research. And MycoGeeky's podcast history is proof that a good conversation can grow into a lasting friendship.</p><a href="/neo-myco/" class="mv-primary">Explore Neo Myco →</a></div>
  </section>
</div>
</Base>